{
  "Appointments over days and hours: day, week, work week and month views, all-day and multi-day bars, appointments at the same time side by side, and \"+N more\" where a day is full. From an array or a data source, with every setting live.": "",
  "Basics": "",
  "Give it the appointments; it reads `startDate`, `endDate`, `text` and `allDay` by default (`fields` names others). The bar moves by the view's step and the date opens a calendar.": "",
  "Views and settings": "",
  "`views` lists the built-in types or views of their own: a name, a caption, an `intervalCount` and settings that win over the scheduler's. Every setting is a value or a function that is followed.": "",
  "With a `DataSource` (REST, OData, a service…) it asks for the days on screen only, and asks again when the view moves. It shows that it is loading, and a retry when a load fails.": "",
  "`appointmentTemplate` draws the content of each appointment; the scheduler still places it, colours it with its `color` and names it for screen readers.": "",
  "Move over the cells (mirrored right to left); past the first or the last day the view moves on. Up from the first time goes to the all-day panel. In the month, Up and Down move by a week.": "",
  "Select from the cell where it began.": "",
  "The first / last day of the row; with Ctrl the first / last cell.": "",
  "A screen of times up / down; in the month, the month before / after.": "",
  "On a cell: double click, click. On an appointment: the same.": "",
  "Clears the selection.": "",
  "The bar, the cells (one Tab stop), the all-day panel, then each appointment.": "",
  "Today, next, previous (option `keys`; not in a text field).": "",
  "Day, week, work week and month view.": "",
  "The times are a `grid` (the all-day panel and the month too) with one Tab stop; each cell is named with its day and time and has `aria-selected`.": "",
  "Buttons in their own group after the cells, named by their time, text and day (\"continues\" when they go on over days).": "",
  "A new date or view is said in a polite live region (`announce`).": "",
  "`aria-busy` while the data source loads; a failed load is an alert with Retry.": "",
  "Dates and times come from `Intl` in its `locale` (12 or 24 hours, the first day of the week); its texts from `uiLocale` (English, Turkish), each one changed with `texts`.": "",
  "The bar.": "",
  "The day views: `data-today`, `data-work`, `data-hour-start`, `aria-selected`.": "",
  "`data-kind=\"timed|bar|chip\"`, `data-before`, `data-after`, `data-short`, `data-past`, `data-disabled`; its colour is `--_color`.": "",
  "\"+N more\", its list, the current time.": "",
  "Units: every piece in its states (a cell: `today`, `off`, `holiday`, `month`, `outside`, `weekend`, `past`, `hover`, `selected`, `focus` …).": "",
  "Sizes, and the shares that mix an appointment's own colour into its fill, its text and its four edges.": "",
  "The appointments in memory. Your data may be plain or reactive; the component reads it as it is. After changing it in place, call `refresh()`. Its own edits (the form, a drag, the methods) show at once.": "",
  "The appointments from `@motifx-community/data`, in place of `appointments`.": "",
  "Asks the data source for the days shown only (a filter on the start and end fields, added to its own).": "",
  "see below": "",
  "The fields it reads: `key`, `start`, `end`, `text`, `allDay`, `description`, `color`, `disabled`, `visible`.": "",
  "day, week, work week, month": "",
  "The views offered. A `SchedulerView` has its own `name`, `text`, `intervalCount`, hours, `cellDuration`, `allDayPanel`, `maxAppointmentsPerCell`.": "",
  "the week": "",
  "The view on screen, by name.": "",
  "today": "",
  "The date the view shows.": "",
  "the locale's": "",
  "Monday–Friday": "",
  "The work week, and the days shaded apart.": "",
  "The work hours; the rest is shaded.": "",
  "The hours the day columns show.": "",
  "Minutes in a cell.": "",
  "The panel of all-day and multi-day appointments over the hours.": "",
  "Lines the all-day panel grows to before \"+N more\".": "",
  "Appointments in a month day before \"+N more\"; `auto`: as many as fit.": "",
  "Appointments at the same time side by side, or each a little to the side.": "",
  "Days marked as holidays.": "",
  "The line at the current time.": "",
  "Appointments that have ended look quieter.": "",
  "work start": "",
  "The hour the day columns scroll to; by default the work start, or now later on today.": "",
  "The bar with today, previous, next, the date and the views.": "",
  "Dates, times and the week.": "",
  "Draws an appointment’s content: `{ appointment, start, end, text, time, allDay, view }`.": "",
  "Its own texts over `uiLocale`.": "",
  "Its keys; an empty list turns one off.": "",
  "Says the new date or view to screen readers.": "",
  "Move the view (asking `onDateChanging`).": "",
  "Show a date, another view.": "",
  "Scrolls the day columns to a time of day.": "",
  "Selects the cells of a time in the days shown.": "",
  "The appointments in a time; one by its key.": "",
  "Reads the appointments and the resources again. Your data may be plain or reactive; the component reads it as it is. After changing it in place, call `refresh()`.": "",
  "Reads one appointment again (an occurrence: its series), after you changed it in place.": "",
  "Reads the resources again: their items, after you changed them in place.": "",
  "Reactive state.": "",
  "A text of `uiLocale` or `texts`, filled in.": "",
  "`{ from, to, byUser, cancel }`: another view; cancel keeps this one.": "",
  "`{ from, to, byUser, cancel }` / `{ …, range }`: today, previous, next, a date chosen.": "",
  "`{ cell: { start, end, allDay }, event, cancel }`; Space and Enter on a cell too.": "",
  "`{ appointment, start, end, event, cancel }`; Space and Enter on an appointment too.": "",
  "`{ selection }`: the selected cells as one time, or `null`.": "",
  "`{ range, appointments }`: after a load, a new date or view, new data.": "",
  "`{ date, appointments, cancel }`: \"+N more\" was pressed; cancel to show the day yourself.": ""
}
